# Page Section Media Preview and Resource Embeds

## Context

Page-section media uses the shared validated media primitive but does not consistently
activate the shared preview lightbox. The builder also cannot yet place existing store
products, forum threads, or documentation sets as page sections.

## Goal

- Make every URL-backed `MediaPlaceholder` keyboard- and pointer-previewable
  through the shared media lightbox by default, including gallery images.
- Add one registered `resource_embed` section with compact resource-type and
  resource dropdowns, bounded public reads,
  resilient loading/error/empty states, and canonical in-app links.
- Preserve the authoritative `pages.content` document model and the existing
  store, forum, and documentation ownership/visibility boundaries.

## Non-Goals

- Do not copy product, thread, or documentation bodies into page JSON.
- Do not add iframe/remote-URL embedding or a second resource API.
- Do not add product mutation, forum participation, or documentation authoring
  controls to embedded sections.

## Steps

1. Make `MediaPlaceholder` directly own its lightbox activation and cover its
   pointer, keyboard, failure-state, opt-out, and teardown behavior.
2. Extend the backend/frontend section registries with one generic
   resource-reference section type.
3. Implement a shared resource-embed renderer that uses existing bounded public
   APIs, exposes picker controls only to page editors, and renders read-only
   linked summaries through existing domain primitives.
4. Add gallery-click, media, renderer, registry, skeleton, picker,
   loading/error, and stale-request regression tests.
5. Reconcile custom-page/frontend/documentation contracts and run the affected
   backend/frontend quality gates.

## Verification

- Backend registry and page compatibility tests, then complete backend suite.
- Focused page-section tests, complete frontend tests, lint, TypeScript, media
  policy, native-dialog policy, production build, and `git diff --check`.
- Todo pairing/status checks and spec reference checks.

